  "body": "`cargo test -p xtask` is red on main: 90 passed, 1 failed.\n\nFailing test: `no_gate_map_names_a_moved_module_as_app` (xtask unit test). Found on origin/main at 7abab8f7, confirmed by two independent agents.\n\nReproduce:\n\n    cargo test -p xtask\n\nWhat fails: the \"Gate map\" headers of two post test suites still name `app::post`, a module that moved to its own crate (`camcraft_post`). The test rejects a gate map that names a moved module as `app::`.\n\nOffending lines:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/grblhal_post.rs:14`: `//! Gate map (#710): covers app::post (grblhal.cps), post::machine`\n- `crates/app/tests/tinyg_post.rs:14`: `//! Gate map: covers app::post (tinyg.cps), post::machine (safeRetractZ, ...`\n\nMerge(s) that introduced it: the files were created by the feat PRs #715 (grblHAL post processor, merged as 11113f72e) and #840 (TinyG post processor, merged as d007f4072). Not determined at the line level: I did not check that the `app::post` header is present in each file's creating commit (24075302 and 83a397d1), only that these are the commits that created the files.\n\nFix: name the owning crate in the two Gate map headers (for example `camcraft_post::post::...`, as AGENTS.md \"A test lives with the code it tests\" asks), so the header names the crate that provides `post`, not `app::post`. Keep the rest of each header unchanged.\n\nDone means: cargo test -p xtask is green on main.\n",
